#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD9727 expect=violation domain=AE
#note "The sister half of the PMDA-SD1380 pair (minted 2026-09-11, M15/T1-34+T1-38). None of USUBJID, APID, SPDEVID and POOLID is in the dataset, so no record can carry a subject, device or pool identifier. The Check is the four not var_exists leaves themselves -- the M15 shape, where the canonical None form runs out because the parent has no remaining condition -- and every leaf is a dataset-level fact, so Sensitivity derives Dataset and the absence is reported ONCE although both rows lack an identifier. Same dataset shape as the parent's skipped_no_identifier_columns scenario: the parent skips, this rule reports."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
dataset AE class=EVENTS label="Adverse Events"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col AESEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col AETERM  type=Char label="Reported Term for the Adverse Event"
---
S1 | AE | 1 | Headache
S1 | AE | 2 | Nausea
